For this lab at first i worked on having a moving yellow stars when the light is bright to make it look
like sun and a white circles to show the moon which we see at night.

then i got suck on finding a way to change the shape with the light and i found out that i can use the 
push, translate, pop, beginShape and endShape functions to do that.
i asked ChatGPT about how to use those functions and it explained to me that
- push will save the current drawing, 
- translate will move the origin to (x, y), and 
- pop will restore everything back
 - beginShape and endShape will create a custom shape based on the vertices defined in between

after i was almost done i realized that i did the wrong assignmnet so i changed it to have only
one star and one moon and not make them move.

i was also add a text to show when the port is not connected
it is a orange text that says "Serial port might be disconnected"